==English==

===Etymology===
From West Indian {{bor|en|es|dengue}} in 1828, from the [[Kiswahili]] term ''dinga'' (in full ''kidingapopo'', "disease caused by an evil spirit"). The borrowed term changed to ''dengue'' in Spanish due to this word existing in Spanish with the meaning "fastidiousness" and this [[folk etymology]] referring to the dislike of movement by affected patients.<ref>[https://web.archive.org/web/20220717162940/https://www.lexico.com/definition/dengue dengue] in Oxford Dictionaries</ref>

===Pronunciation===
* {{a|GenAm}} {{IPA|en|/ˈdɛŋɡi/|/ˈdɛŋɡeɪ/}}
* {{a|UK}} {{IPA|en|/ˈdɛŋɡi/}}
* {{audio|en|LL-Q1860 (eng)-Vealhurl-dengue.wav|Audio (Southern England)}}
* {{lb|en|Indian English}} {{IPA|en|/ˈɖɛŋɡi/|/ˈɖɛŋɡʊ/}}
* {{lb|en|Philippine English}} {{IPA|en|/ˈɖɛŋɡɛ/}}
* {{rhymes|en|ɛŋɡi|ɛŋɡeɪ|q2=General American|s=2}}

===Noun===
{{en-noun|-|s}}

# An [[acute]] [[febrile]] [[disease]] of the (sub)[[tropic]]s caused by the ''[[Dengue virus]]'', a [[flavivirus]], transmitted by ''[[Aedes]]'' [[mosquito]]es, and characterized by high [[fever]], [[rash]], [[headache]], and [[severe]] [[muscle]] and [[joint]] [[pain]].

